Why not use only one model?

Because a model optimised for portraits is not necessarily good at separating shoes, furniture, bottles, cars or other products.

Your app should intelligently choose the correct engine:

| Uploaded image      | Processing engine                         |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Human portrait      | Selfie segmentation                       |
| Hair-heavy portrait | Person + hair refinement                  |
| Product image       | Interactive object segmentation           |
| Multiple objects    | Interactive selection + manual refinement |
| Difficult image     | Manual erase/restore fallback             |

For a later high-quality server engine, evaluate BiRefNet and its appropriate variants. It is a potential advanced model, but you will need model hosting, hardware and licence verification before commercial deployment.

The quality rule: Always preserve the original-resolution image and apply the generated mask to that image. Never export only the small resized preview used for AI inference.

## 5. Database design

Use Firebase Firestore initially.

Your database should have the following structure:

| Collection     | Information                      |
| -------------- | -------------------------------- |
| users          | User profile and settings        |
| projects       | Project name, owner, timestamps  |
| images         | Original dimensions and metadata |
| processingJobs | Status, engine, errors, duration |
| editSessions   | Brush and background settings    |
| subscriptions  | Plan and subscription status     |
| usage          | Processing and export counts     |

Example project record:

```
{
  "projectId": "project_001",
  "userId": "authenticated_user_id",
  "name": "Product Photo",
  "originalWidth": 4000,
  "originalHeight": 3000,
  "engine": "mediapipe",
  "status": "completed",
  "exportFormat": "png",
  "createdAt": "server_timestamp"
}
```

This is a suggested schema, not a record you need to enter manually.

Privacy and security rules:

- Users can access only their own projects.
- Never trust a user ID supplied by the client without authentication.
- Validate every upload.
- Keep private images private.
- Do not store API secrets in the APK.
- Add account and image deletion.
- Avoid storing original images permanently unless the user chooses to save them.

